wayvnc is a VNC server for wlroots-based Wayland compositors. It
attaches to a running Wayland session, creates virtual input devices,
and exposes a display (or multiple outputs) over the RFB protocol.

It supports screencopy, GPU-side dmabuf capture, TLS/VeNCrypt (via
neatvnc), PAM authentication, and a control socket (wayvncctl) for
runtime configuration.

Requirements (all part of the Slackware base system):
  - meson
  - ninja
  - pixman
  - libdrm
  - gbm
  - libxkbcommon
  - wayland
  - jansson
  - Linux-PAM
  - scdoc (man pages)

SBo dependencies:
  - aml
  - neatvnc
